      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has been my experience as of late too - seems like both world and avatar can affect this, with some avatars consistently producing a multi-second lag somewhere during avatar load (while it's still a blue diamond), and some worlds causing every avatar to produce a shorter but still noticeable load lag. Two worlds where I noticed this are `wrld_61021c2e-c69c-41b3-a000-6426ef5cdb05` and `wrld_c3bd482e-5f44-4d49-99e1-b6a5e7d6c17d`.\n\nAs we may not attach a profiler or use a debug player for profiling (thanks EAC!), and can't meaningfully use ETW profiling due to lack of debug symbols (thanks weird non-public DWR builds of unity!), collecting actually useful information is left as an exercise for the reader.\n\nAMD Ryzen 5800X3D, 7900XTX, freshly installed windows (thanks EAC!), plenty of RAM and fast SSDs.\n\nRelevant log lines (4 seconds worth of load lag from an avatar that is otherwise fine!):\n\n```\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:51 Log        -  [AssetBundleDownloadManager] Unpacking Download\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:55 Warning    -  [Behaviour] Avatar has 1 colliders. These will add an additional performance cost when active and no mirrors/cameras are active.\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:55 Warning    -  [Behaviour] Avatar has 1 colliders. These will add an additional performance cost when active and no mirrors/cameras are active.\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  [Behaviour] CacheComponents: ParticleSystems 0, AudioSources 1\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  Found SDK3 avatar descriptor.\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  [Behaviour] Using custom gesture mask from base layer\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  [Behaviour] Using custom fx mask\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  Measure Human Avatar Avatar isRemeasure:False\n\n2023.09.23 00:53:56 Log        -  [Behaviour] Initialize ThreePoint Avatar (UnityEngine.Animator) VRCPlayer[Remote] 16840828 6 (ÎÌÎÌÏÎÎÍÏÎÍÌÏÏÍÎÌÍÌÍÏÌÍ) False Custom\n\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
